  ],
  "description": "Analog reconstruction of one channel of the early Manley Massive Passive Standard, from its published original manual. Four parallel passive LC sections use the original selectable frequency sets, separate boost/cut buses, damping controls and opposite-section resonant overlays for shelving. Select Cut or Band Out separately. The highest active frequency wins within a band; all frequency switches off selects its lowest frequency. Passive end filters sit between the two estimated tube makeup stages and use equivalent ladder values and isolation buffers. Each makeup stage has a 12AX7A proxy for 5751 and two direct-coupled 12BH7A models for the 6414 current-gain pair. The transformer and tertiary feedback, intermediate termination, input NE5532 proxy, powers and passive part values are estimates. The 22/33 Hz and 16/27 kHz shelf voicings, exact end-filter ripples and inductor saturation remain outside this reconstruction.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
